{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To determine how many prime numbers must be multiplied to make 2400, we start by finding the prime factorization of 2400.\n\n1. **Prime Factorization of 2400:**\n   - First, we divide 2400 by the smallest prime number, which is 2.\n     \\[\n     2400 \\div 2 = 1200\n     \\]\n   - We continue dividing by 2:\n     \\[\n     1200 \\div 2 = 600\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     600 \\div 2 = 300\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     300 \\div 2 = 150\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     150 \\div 2 = 75\n     \\]\n   - Now, 75 is not divisible by 2, so we move to the next smallest prime number, which is 3.\n     \\[\n     75 \\div 3 = 25\n     \\]\n   - Next, 25 is not divisible by 3, so we move to the next smallest prime number, which is 5.\n     \\[\n     25 \\div 5 = 5\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     5 \\div 5 = 1\n     \\]\n\n","prefix_end":747,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,8253,1246,1657,10250,5109,1969,387,54916,311,1281,220,17,19,15,15,11,582,1191,553,9271,279,10250,8168,2022,315,220,17,19,15,15,382,16,13,3070,32306,37729,2022,315,220,17,19,15,15,25,1019,256,481,5512,11,582,21749,220,17,19,15,15,553,279,24632,10250,1372,11,892,374,220,17,624,257,1124,9640,257,220,17,19,15,15,1124,611,220,17,284,220,16,17,15,15,198,257,1124,921,256,481,1205,3060,49702,553,220,17,510,257,1124,9640,257,220,16,17,15,15,1124,611,220,17,284,220,21,15,15,198,257,1124,921,257,1124,9640,257,220,21,15,15,1124,611,220,17,284,220,18,15,15,198,257,1124,921,257,1124,9640,257,220,18,15,15,1124,611,220,17,284,220,16,20,15,198,257,1124,921,257,1124,9640,257,220,16,20,15,1124,611,220,17,284,220,22,20,198,257,1124,921,256,481,4695,11,220,22,20,374,537,74916,553,220,17,11,773,582,3271,311,279,1790,24632,10250,1372,11,892,374,220,18,624,257,1124,9640,257,220,22,20,1124,611,220,18,284,220,17,20,198,257,1124,921,256,481,9295,11,220,17,20,374,537,74916,553,220,18,11,773,582,